  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`, but I couldn't verify it. `@aura3d/engine` is missing from this sandbox (`node_modules/@aura3d/` is empty), so `typecheck` fails with TS2307 (cannot find module) and a follow-on implicit-any error on the `onFrame` parameter. I never ran the scene or `vite build`. I also couldn't read the package types, so I wrote the material option names (`transmission`, `ior`, `thickness`, `anisotropy`) from the docs and by inference. They may need adjusting once the package is installed.\n\n- **Studio:** A generated floor curves up into the backdrop through a quarter-circle cove. The three spheres sit in a row on it. The camera is fixed, raised and three-quarter-front.\n- **Lighting:** There is a shadow-casting key light, a dimmer fill from the opposite side, a rim light from behind, an `environments.studio` reflection source, and contact shadows.\n- **Glass (left):** It uses `material.glass`, with transmission, a refractive index (ior) of 1.5, low roughness and partial opacity.\n- **Metal (centre):** It uses `material.brushedMetal`, fully metallic with an anisotropic, blurred reflection.\n- **Fabric (right):** It is a custom GLSL dark-red velvet with a procedural weave, fibre noise and a grazing sheen. It has no mirror reflection and is lit by the same key, fill and rim.\n- **Animation:** The key light drifts side to side as `6·sin(0.4t)`. The same value drives the fabric shader.\n- **State and flags:** `window.__TASK_STATE__` is updated every frame. `__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` plus two animation frames.\n\n",
